rt WHO HIV care and monitoring guidelines','en',3,'2015-12-21 11:32:13',NULL,NULL,'8d01f270-cae0-492c-afb3-a51f1a306171'),(3311,99891,'This concept added to support WHO HIV care and monitoring guidelines','en',3,'2015-12-21 11:33:08',NULL,NULL,'5125cd9d-cfb0-4e26-a57f-4bc3ce1fedad'),(3312,99892,'This concept added to support WHO HIV care and monitoring guidelines','en',3,'2015-12-21 11:33:58',NULL,NULL,'bb13a85c-8739-45bf-9700-8c3e6ea94de9'),(3329,112416,'Condition of vaginal bleeding with or without pain in early pregnancy which may presage an abortion.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'3329FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3368,112561,'Traumatic injuries involving the cranium and intracranial structures (i.e., BRAIN; CRANIAL NERVES; MENINGES; and other structures). Injuries may be classified by whether or not the skull is penetrated (i.e., penetrating vs. nonpenetrating) or whether there is an associated hemorrhage.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'3368FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3499,112989,'A pathological condition that can suddenly affect the hemodynamic equilibrium, usually manifested by failure to perfuse or oxygenate vital organs.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-12-31 21:11:25','3499FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3500,112992,'Diseases due to or propagated by sexual contact.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-07-10 03:05:27','3500FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3599,113230,'The most important manifestation of and sequel to rheumatic fever, i.e., any cardiac involvement in rheumatic fever. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'3599FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3676,113489,'Tuberculosis of the lungs.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'3676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3678,113491,'Tuberculosis of the lungs.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'3678FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3789,113705,'Tumors or cancer of the MOUTH.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'3789FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3800,113729,'Tumors or cancer of the COLON.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'3800FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3854,113881,'Anxiety disorders manifested by the development of characteristic symptoms following a psychologically traumatic event that is outside the normal range of usual human experience. Symptoms include re-experiencing the traumatic event and numbing of responsiveness to or reduced involvement with the external world.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-05-27 03:00:56','3854FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3911,114100,'Inflammation of the lungs.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:06:58',1,'2015-11-03 03:04:09','3911FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3918,114120,'An acute infectious disease caused by YERSINIA PESTIS that affects humans, wild rodents, and their ectoparasites. This condition persists due to its firm entrenchment in sylvatic rodent-flea ecosystems throughout the world. Bubonic plague is the most common form.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'3918FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3920,114127,'A placenta which develops in the lower uterine segment, in the zone of dilatation, so that it covers or adjoins the internal os. Painless hemorrhage in the last trimester, particularly during the eighth month, is the most common symptom. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'3920FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(3941,114174,'Inflammation of a vein associated with thrombus formation.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'3941FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4028,114413,'Increase in body weight beyond skeletal and physical standards as the result of an excessive accumulation of fat in the body. More than two times the ideal weight is considered OBESITY, MORBID.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4028FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4289,115355,'Tumors or cancer of the MOUTH.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4289FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4296,115368,'A transient unconjugated hyperbilirubinemia that occurs between the second and fifth days of life because the hepatic enzyme GLUCURONOSYLTRANSFERASE required for BILIRUBIN detoxification is inadquedate.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4296FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4485,115797,'Generic term for diseases caused by an abnormal metabolic process. It can be congenital due to inherited enzyme abnormality (METABOLISM, INBORN ERRORS) or acquired due to disease of an endocrine organ or failure of a metabolically important organ such as the liver. (Stedman, 26th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'4485FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4501,115835,'Inflammation of the coverings of the brain and/or spinal cord, which consist of the PIA MATER; ARACHNOID; and DURA MATER. Infections (viral, bacterial, and fungal) are the most common causes of this condition, but subarachnoid hemorrhage (HEMORRHAGES, SUBARACHNOID), chemical irritation (chemical MENINGITIS), granulomatous conditions, neoplastic conditions (e.g., carcinomatous meningitis), and other inflammatory conditions may produce this syndrome. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1994, Ch24, p6)','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:02:40',1,'2016-05-27 20:34:04','4501FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4566,116023,'Tumors or cancer of the uterine cervix.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4566FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4569,116026,'Tumors or cancer of the breast.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4569FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4639,116128,'A protozoan disease caused by four species of the genus PLASMODIUM (P. falciparum (MALARIA, FALCIPARUM), P. vivax (MALARIA, VIVAX), P. ovale, and P. malariae) and transmitted by the bite of an infected female mosquito of the genus Anopheles. Malaria is endemic in parts of Asia, Africa, Central and South America, Oceania, and certain Caribbean islands. It is characterized by extreme exhaustion associated with paroxysms of high fever, sweating, shaking chills, and anemia.','en',1,'2007-11-02 19:28:08',1,'2018-12-05 08:13:08','4639FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4676,116214,'Abnormally low blood pressure seen in shock but not necessarily indicative of it. (Dorland, 28th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'4676FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4713,116350,'A disease caused by any of a number of species of protozoa in the genus LEISHMANIA. There are four major clinical types of this infection: cutaneous (Old and New World) (LEISHMANIASIS, CUTANEOUS), diffuse cutaneous (LEISHMANIASIS, DIFFUSE CUTANEOUS), mucocutaneous (LEISHMANIASIS, MUCOCUTANEOUS), and visceral (LEISHMANIASIS, VISCERAL).','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4713FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4719,116376,'A sudden, nonconvulsive loss of neurologic function due to an ischemic or hemorrhagic intracranial vascular event. In general, cerebrovascular accidents are classified by anatomic location in the brain, vascular distribution, etiology, age of the affected individual, and hemorrhagic vs. nonhemorrhagic nature. (From Adams et al., Principles of Neurology, 6th ed, pp777-810)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'4719FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4745,116474,'The lack of sufficient energy or protein to meet the body\'s metabolic demands, as a result of either an inadequate dietary intake of protein, intake of poor quality dietary protein, increased demands due to disease, or increased nutrient losses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2014-10-03 17:17:41','4745FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4775,116543,'Injuries to tissues caused by contact with heat, steam, chemicals (BURNS, CHEMICAL), electricity (BURNS, ELECTRIC), or the like.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'4775FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4802,116608,'A disorder of cardiac function caused by insufficient blood flow to the muscle tissue of the heart. The decreased blood flow may be due to narrowing of the coronary arteries (CORONARY ARTERIOSCLEROSIS), to obstruction by a thrombus (CORONARY THROMBOSIS), or less commonly, to diffuse narrowing of arterioles and other small vessels within the heart. Severe interruption of the blood supply to the myocardial tissue may result in necrosis of cardiac muscle (MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION).','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4802FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4831,116700,'Infestation with parasitic worms of the helminth class.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'4831FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4853,116758,'Bites and stings inflicted by insects.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'4853FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4929,117146,'Infections in birds and mammals produced by various species of Trichomonas.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2014-10-03 17:21:26','4929FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4933,117152,'SCHISTOSOMIASE','fr',1,'2007-09-06 09:05:28',1,NULL,'4933FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(4978,117315,'The condition that results from excessive loss of body water.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'4978FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5005,117386,'Hypertrophy or enlargement of the heart.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5005FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5011,117399,'Persistently high arterial blood pressure. Currently accepted threshold levels are 140 mm Hg systolic and 90 mm Hg diastolic pressure.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-11-03 02:49:23','5011FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5047,117474,'A circumscribed collection of fluid, especially a collection of fluid in the tunica vaginalis of the testicle or along the spermatic cord. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5047FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5143,117698,'A condition in which the sense of hearing, although defective, is functional with or without a hearing aid. The hearing loss may affect one or both ears. The normal hearing level for speech is approximately 40-70 decibels I.S.O. (International Organization for Standardization) or 30-60 db A.S.A. (American Standards Association).','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5143FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5147,117703,'A disease characterized by chronic hemolytic anemia, episodic painful crises, and pathologic involvement of many organs. It is the clinical expression of homozygosity for hemoglobin S.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5147FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5187,117789,'An ocular disease, occurring in many forms, having as its primary characteristics an unstable or a sustained increase in the intraocular pressure which the eye cannot withstand without damage to its structure or impairment of its function. The consequences of the increased pressure may be manifested in a variety of symptoms, depending upon type and severity, such as excavation of the optic disk, hardness of the eyeball, corneal anesthesia, reduced visual acuity, seeing of colored halos around lights, disturbed dark adaptation, visual field defects, and headaches. (Dictionary of Visual Science, 4th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5205,117829,'Herpes simplex of the genitals.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5205FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5228,117889,'Inflammation of the lining of the stomach and intestines, often accompanied by diarrhea.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:20:58',1,'2016-05-25 20:46:33','5228FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5445,118652,'Cerebral tissue herniation through a congenital or acquired defect in the skull. The majority of congenital encephaloceles occur in the occipital or frontal regions. Clinical features include a protuberant mass that may be pulsatile. The quantity and location of protruding neural tissue determines the type and degree of neurologic deficit. Visual defects, psychomotor developmental delay, and persistent motor deficits frequently occur.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5445FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5475,118744,'Onset of convulsions or coma in a previously diagnosed pre-eclamptic patient.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5475FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5495,118789,'Difficulty in swallowing.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:15:17',1,'2015-12-31 16:53:40','5495FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5516,118855,'Illegitimate use of drugs for a desired effect in humans or animals. Not specified whether use is episodic, chronic, or in remission.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5516FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5556,118939,'Visual impairments limiting one or more of the basic functions of the eye: visual acuity, dark adaptation, color vision, or peripheral vision. These may result from EYE DISEASES; OPTIC NERVE DISEASES; VISUAL PATHWAY diseases; OCCIPITAL LOBE diseases; OCULAR MOTILITY DISORDERS; and other conditions. Visual disability refers to inability of the individual to perform specific visual tasks, such as reading, writing, orientation, or traveling unaided. (From Newell, Ophthalmology: Principles and Concepts, 7th ed, p132)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5556FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5583,119056,'Deviations from the average or standard indices of refraction of the eye through its dioptric or refractive apparatus.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5583FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5600,119112,'Diseases of the central and peripheral nervous system. This includes disorders of the brain, spinal cord, cranial nerves, peripheral nerves, nerve roots, autonomic nervous system, neuromuscular junction, and muscle.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5600FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5623,119204,'The state of the body in relation to the intake and excretion of water and electrolytes, particularly sodium and potassium. It exists in a metabolic balance internally with BODY FLUID COMPARTMENTS, total BODY WATER, BLOOD VOLUME, EXTRACELLULAR SPACE, etc., externally through sensible and insensible SWEATING. The hypothalamus controls water balance. (Dorland, 27th ed; Mountcastle, Medical Physiology, 14th ed, 1980, p1152)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5623FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5626,119240,'Diseases of the ear, general or unspecified.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5626FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5634,119270,'DEF: Disease of the cardiovascular system, that is, the heart and blood vessels.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5634FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5662,119356,'Infection of humans or animals with hookworms other than those caused by the genus Ancylostoma or Necator, for which the specific terms ANCYLOSTOMIASIS and NECATORIASIS are available.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5662FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5733,119481,'A heterogeneous group of disorders that share glucose intolerance in common.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:10:30',NULL,NULL,'5733FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5734,119483,'Conditions characterized by language abilities (comprehension and expression of speech and writing) that are below the expected level for a given age, generally in the absence of an intellectual impairment. These conditions may be associated with DEAFNESS; BRAIN DISEASES; MENTAL DISORDERS; or environmental factors.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5734FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5743,119506,'Superficial infections of the skin or its appendages by any of various fungi.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5743FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5750,119523,'Superficial infections of the skin or its appendages by any of various fungi.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5750FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5764,119558,'Localized destruction of the tooth surface initiated by decalcification of the enamel followed by enzymatic lysis of organic structures and leading to cavity formation. If left unchecked, the cavity may penetrate the enamel and dentin and reach the pulp. The three most prominent theories used to explain the etiology of the disase are that acids produced by bacteria lead to decalcification; that micro-organisms destroy the enamel protein; or that keratolytic micro-organisms produce chelates that lead to decalcification.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:08:47',1,'2011-12-22 18:39:36','5764FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5785,119656,'An ulceration caused by prolonged pressure in patients permitted to lie too still for a long period of time. The bony prominences of the body are the most frequently affected sites. The ulcer is caused by ischemia of the underlying structures of the skin, fat, and muscles as a result of the sustained and constant pressure.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5785FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5799,119685,'Inflammation of the urinary bladder. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'5799FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5885,119964,'Accidents on streets, roads, and highways involving drivers, passengers, pedestrians, or vehicles. Traffic accidents refer to AUTOMOBILES (passenger cars, buses, and trucks), BICYCLING, and MOTORCYCLES but not OFF-ROAD MOTOR VEHICLES, RAILROADS nor snowmobiles.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'5885FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5923,120147,'Sexually transmitted form of anogenital warty growth caused by the human papillomaviruses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2013-05-05 22:00:41','5923FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5924,120148,'Any variation from the normal rhythm or rate of the heart beat.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-11-05 01:33:05','5924FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(5938,120194,'Disorders or diseases associated with the six-to-eight-week period immediately following labor and delivery.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-10-01 07:54:30','5938FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6267,121131,'A major affective disorder marked by severe mood swings (manic or major depressive episodes) and a tendency to remission and recurrence.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'6267FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6313,121262,'Infections by bacteria, general or unspecified.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-06-19 20:32:03','6313FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6363,121372,'A sudden intense and continuous aggravation of a state of asthma, marked by dyspnea to the point of exhaustion and collapse and not responding to the usual therapeutic efforts.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2014-12-22 22:22:05','6363FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6366,121375,'ugonjwa wa pumu','sw',1,'2007-12-11 21:17:36',1,'2015-11-03 02:47:41','6366FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6373,121397,'A pathological condition caused by lack of oxygen, manifested in impending or actual cessation of life.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'6373FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6419,121540,'Disorders in which anxiety (persistent feelings of apprehension, tension, or uneasiness) is the predominant disturbance.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'6419FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6449,121629,'A reduction in the number of circulating erythrocytes or in the quantity of hemoglobin.','en',1,'2007-10-14 11:31:45',1,'2015-11-05 01:29:33','6449FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6450,121629,'ugonjwa wa kuvuja damu','sw',1,'2007-12-11 19:33:36',1,'2015-11-05 01:29:33','6450FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6494,121725,'A primary, chronic disease with genetic, psychosocial, and environmental factors influencing its development and manifestations. The disease is often progressive and fatal. It is characterized by impaired control over drinking, preoccupation with the drug alcohol, use of alcohol despite adverse consequences, and distortions in thinking, most notably denial. Each of these symptoms may be continuous or periodic. (Morse & Flavin for the Joint Commission of the National Council on Alcoholism and Drug Dependence and the American Society of Addiction Medicine to Study the Definition and Criteria for the Diagnosis of Alcoholism: in JAMA 1992;268:1012-4)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'6494FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6495,121725,'kupiga vita pombe','sw',1,'2007-12-11 21:14:44',NULL,NULL,'6495FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6700,122496,'Difficult or labored breathing.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'6700FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6722,122604,'An acute diarrheal disease endemic in India and Southeast Asia whose causative agent is VIBRIO CHOLERAE. This condition can lead to severe dehydration in a matter of hours unless quickly treated.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2018-05-01 16:26:59','6722FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6863,122983,'The forcible expulsion of the contents of the stomach through the mouth.','en',1,'2007-11-02 19:46:00',NULL,NULL,'6863FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6890,123052,'A nutritional condition produced by a deficiency of VITAMIN A in the diet, characterized by NIGHT BLINDNESS and other ocular manifestations such as dryness of the conjunctiva and later of the cornea (XEROPHTHALMIA). Vitamin A deficiency is a very common problem worldwide, particularly in developing countries as a consequence of famine or shortages of vitamin A-rich foods. In the United States it is found among the urban poor, the elderly, alcoholics, and patients with malabsorption. (From Cecil Textbook of Medicine, 19th ed, p1179)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'6890FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6926,123112,'A group of viral diseases of diverse etiology but having many similar clinical characteristics; increased capillary permeability, leukopenia, and thrombocytopenia are common to all. Hemorrhagic fevers are characterized by sudden onset, fever, headache, generalized myalgia, backache, conjunctivitis, and severe prostration, followed by various hemorrhagic symptoms. Hemorrhagic fever with kidney involvement is HEMORRHAGIC FEVER WITH RENAL SYNDROME.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'6926FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(6933,123123,'Inflammation, often mild, of the conjunctiva caused by a variety of viral agents. Conjunctival involvement may be part of a systemic infection.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'6933FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7057,123493,'Schistosomiasis caused by SCHISTOSOMA HAEMATOBIUM. It is endemic in Africa and parts of the Middle East, and affects the urinary tract.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'7057FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7066,123529,'DEF: Discharge of purulent fluid from the urethra. DESC: Commonly caused by Gonorrhea and/or chlamydia. REF: Merck Manual','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-05-21 14:00:44','7066FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7067,123529,'ECOULEMENT URETRAL','fr',1,'2007-07-13 14:56:43',1,'2016-05-21 14:00:44','7067FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7154,123815,'The lack of sufficient energy or protein to meet the body\'s metabolic demands, as a result of either an inadequate dietary intake of protein, intake of poor quality dietary protein, increased demands due to disease, or increased nutrient losses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'7154FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7275,124129,'Infection with nematodes of the genus TRICHURIS, formerly called Trichocephalus.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'7275FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7718,125872,'Death of the young developing in utero.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'7718FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7773,126127,'Expulsion of the products of conception before the completion of gestation without deliberate interference.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'7773FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7801,126208,'Congenital defects of closure of one or more vertebral arches, which may be associated with malformations of the spinal cord, nerve roots, congenital fibrous bands, lipomas, and congenital cysts. These malformations range from mild (e.g., SPINA BIFIDA OCCULTA) to severe, including rachischisis where there is complete failure of neural tube and spinal cord fusion, resulting in exposure of the spinal cord at the surface. Spinal dysraphism includes all forms of spina bifida. The open form is called SPINA BIFIDA CYSTICA and the closed form is SPINA BIFIDA OCCULTA. (From Joynt, Clinical Neurology, 1992, Ch55, p34)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'7801FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7838,126323,'The condition of having been bitten by a snake (not specified if venomous or non-venomous), characterized by stinging pain at the wound puncture. ','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'7838FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7914,126558,'An infectious disease caused by bacteria of the genus SHIGELLA. This condition is characterized by intestinal pain and diarrhea.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'7914FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(7930,126598,'The lack of sufficient energy or protein to meet the body\'s metabolic demands, as a result of either an inadequate dietary intake of protein, intake of poor quality dietary protein, increased demands due to disease, or increased nutrient losses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'7930FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(8328,127579,'The persistence to perform a learned behavior (facts or experiences) after an interval has elapsed in which there has been no performance or practice of the behavior.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'8328FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(8376,127750,'Patient or client refusal of or resistance to medical, psychological, or psychiatric treatment. (APA, Thesaurus of Psychological Index Terms, 8th ed.)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'8376FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(8452,127990,'Fever in which the etiology cannot be ascertained.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:16:08',1,'2016-05-27 02:00:14','8452FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(8508,128126,'Bronchial hemorrhage manifested with spitting of blood.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'8508FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(8973,129251,'Development of hypertension with proteinuria, edema, or both, due to pregnancy or the influence of a recent pregnancy. It occurs after the 20th week of gestation, but it may develop before this time in the presence of trophoblastic disease.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'8973FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9072,129566,'A developmental anomaly characterized by the presence of more than five fingers on the hand or more than five toes on the foot in primates. In non-primate vertebrates, it refers to the presence of more than the normal number of toes on the forelimb or hindlimb. (Dorland, 27th ed; Stedman, 25th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'9072FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9144,130108,'Premature separation of the normally implanted placenta.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'9144FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9270,130576,'A recurrent disease of the oral mucosa of unknown etiology. It is characterized by small white ulcerative lesions, single or multiple, round or oval. Two to eight crops of lesions occur per year, lasting for 7 to 14 days and then heal without scarring. (From Jablonski\'s Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p742)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'9270FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9467,131113,'Inflammation of the middle ear.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:16:26',1,NULL,'9467FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9468,131113,'Otite moyenne','fr',1,'2007-09-06 08:51:25',1,NULL,'9468FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9762,132636,'A syndrome produced by severe protein deficiency, characterized by retarded growth, changes in skin and hair pigment, edema, and pathologic changes in the liver, including fatty infiltration, necrosis, and fibrosis. The word is a local name in Gold Coast, Africa, meaning displaced child. Although first reported from Africa, kwashiorkor is now known throughout the world, but mainly in the tropics and subtropics. It is considered to be related to marasmus. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'9762FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9763,132636,'MARASME','fr',1,'2007-07-13 13:53:41',1,NULL,'9763FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9837,133027,'Sleep hyperhidrosis, more commonly known as the night sweats, is the occurrence of excessive sweating (hyperhidrosis) during sleep. The sufferer may or may not also suffer from excessive perspiration while awake. Sleep hyperhidrosis may occur at any age, but is most commonly seen in early adulthood.\r\nref: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_sweats','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:10:01',NULL,NULL,'9837FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(9975,133328,'Tumors or cancer of the LUNG.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'9975FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10003,133414,'Acute conjunctival inflammation in the newborn, usually caused by maternal gonococcal infection. The baby\'s eyes are contaminated during passage through the birth canal.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'10003FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10318,134213,'Abnormal smallness of the head, usually associated with mental retardation. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-08-01 19:24:17','10318FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10354,134337,'Psychiatric illness or diseases manifested by breakdowns in the adaptational process expressed primarily as abnormalities of thought, feeling, and behavior producing either distress or impairment of function.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-11-04 04:38:38','10354FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10416,134561,'A highly contagious infectious disease caused by MORBILLIVIRUS, common among children but also seen in the nonimmune of any age, in which the virus enters the respiratory tract via droplet nuclei and multiplies in the epithelial cells, spreading throughout the reticuloendothelial system. (From Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:12:00',1,'2016-07-29 22:53:57','10416FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10452,134722,'The lack of sufficient energy or protein to meet the body\'s metabolic demands, as a result of either an inadequate dietary intake of protein, intake of poor quality dietary protein, increased demands due to disease, or increased nutrient losses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'10452FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10453,134723,'The lack of sufficient energy or protein to meet the body\'s metabolic demands, as a result of either an inadequate dietary intake of protein, intake of poor quality dietary protein, increased demands due to disease, or increased nutrient losses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'10453FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10847,135462,'Subacute inflammation of the inguinal lymph glands caused by certain immunotypes of CHLAMYDIA TRACHOMATIS. It is a sexually transmitted disease in the U.S. but is more widespread in developing countries. It is distinguished from granuloma venereum (see GRANULOMA INGUINALE), which is caused by Calymmatobacterium granulomatis.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'10847FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10856,135480,'Edema due to obstruction of lymph vessels or disorders of the lymph nodes.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'10856FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10905,135595,'Clinical manifestation consisting of a physiopathological lack or loss of appetite accompanied by an aversion to food and the inability to eat.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'10905FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(10924,135721,'Primary carcinoma of the liver cells. It ranges from a well-differentiated tumor difficult to distinguish from normal hepatocytes to a poorly differentiated neoplasm. The cells may be uniform or markedly pleomorphic or may form giant cells. Several classification schemes have been suggested.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'10924FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11078,136162,'Acidosis caused by accumulation of lactic acid more rapidly than it can be metabolized. It may occur spontaneously or in association with diseases such as diabetes mellitus, leukemia, or liver failure.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'11078FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11171,136443,'DEF:Yellow pigmentation of the skin and sclerae due to a raised level of plasma bilirubin. DESC: classified by the type of circulating bilirubin (conjugated or uncongugated). REF OXFORD CLINICAL MEDICINE','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:02:04',1,'2015-12-31 16:44:51','11171FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11245,136675,'Schistosomiasis caused by Schistosoma mansoni. It is endemic in Africa, the Middle East, South America, and the Caribbean and affects mainly the bowel, spleen, and liver.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'11245FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11247,136677,'Infections of the intestines with a parasite. They are caused most commonly by intestinal nematodes (roundworms) and cestodes (tapeworms). (From Merck Manual, 15th ed; Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-11-03 03:02:46','11247FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11276,136758,'Uterine bleeding, usually irregular or acyclic, between periods.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'11276FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11369,137293,'Skin diseases caused by bacteria, fungi, parasites, or viruses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'11369FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11404,137352,'A genus of large tapeworms.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'11404FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11406,137355,'Infection with nematodes of the genus STRONGYLOIDES. The presence of larvae may produce pneumonitis and the presence of adult worms in the intestine could lead to moderate to severe diarrhea.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'11406FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11419,137393,'Infection with nematodes of the genus ONCHOCERCA. Characteristics include the presence of firm subcutaneous nodules filled with adult worms, pruritus, and ocular lesions.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'11419FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11450,137458,'A genus of nematode parasites which inhabit the body cavity, serous membranes, and connective tissues of vertebrates. The species parasitic in man is Dracunculus medinensis.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'11450FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11759,138291,'Abnormally increased content of sugar in the blood. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-06-24 02:01:09','11759FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11958,138680,'A recurrent disease of the oral mucosa of unknown etiology. It is characterized by small white ulcerative lesions, single or multiple, round or oval. Two to eight crops of lesions occur per year, lasting for 7 to 14 days and then heal without scarring. (From Jablonski\'s Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p742)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'11958FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(11981,138706,'A group of acute infections caused by herpes simplex virus type 1 or type 2 that is characterized by the development of one or more small fluid-filled vesicles with a raised erythematous base on the skin or mucous membrane. It occurs as a primary infection or recurs due to a reactivation of a latent infection. (Dorland, 27th ed.)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2012-06-06 18:30:47','11981FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12058,138849,'Varicosities of the hemorrhoidal venous plexuses.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-11-04 04:07:14','12058FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12062,138868,'Any of various disorders marked by inflammation of the intestines, especially of the colon, and attended by pain in the abdomen, tenesmus, and frequent stools containing blood and mucus. Causes include chemical irritants, bacteria, protozoa, or parasitic worms. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-05-25 20:42:13','12062FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12134,139069,'Heart decompensation in which the heart is unable to maintain adequate circulation of blood in the tissues of the body or to pump out the venous blood returned to it by the venous circulation.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'12134FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12141,139084,'Pain in the cranial region that may occur as an isolated and benign symptom or as a manifestation of a wide variety of conditions including SUBARACHNOID HEMORRHAGE; CRANIOCEREBRAL TRAUMA; CENTRAL NERVOUS SYSTEM INFECTIONS; INTRACRANIAL HYPERTENSION; and other disorders. In general, recurrent headaches that are not associated with a primary disease process are referred to as HEADACHE DISORDERS (e.g., MIGRAINE).','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:20:16',1,'2015-11-05 01:38:54','12141FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12204,139277,'Anogenital ulcers caused by Calymmatobacterium granulomatis as distinguished from lymphogranuloma inguinale (see LYMPHOGRANULOMA VENEREUM) caused by CHLAMYDIA TRACHOMATIS. Diagnosis is made by demonstration of typical intracellular Donovan bodies in crushed-tissue smears.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'12204FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12250,139355,'The presence of glucose in the urine, especially the excretion of an abnormally large amount of sugar (glucose) in the urine. (Dorland, 27th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'12250FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12515,140039,'A transient reddening of the face that may be due to fever, certain drugs, exertion, stress, or a disease process.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'12515FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12547,140144,'One of several skin tests to determine past or present tuberculosis infection. A purified protein derivative of the tubercle bacilli, called tuberculin, is introduced into the skin by scratch, puncture, or interdermal injection.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'12547FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12569,140238,'An abnormal elevation of body temperature, usually as a result of a pathologic process.','en',1,'2007-11-02 19:43:33',1,'2015-11-05 01:37:17','12569FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12730,140987,'Persistently high arterial blood pressure. Currently accepted threshold levels are 140 mm Hg systolic and 90 mm Hg diastolic pressure.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'12730FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12832,141216,'A genus of intestinal nematode worms which includes the pinworm or threadworm Enterobius vermicularis.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'12832FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(12998,141723,'Acute hepatitis caused by true hepatotoxins such as Amanita phaloides toxin, carbon tetrachloride, yellow phosphorus, and a variety of drugs. (From Dorland, 28th ed)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'12998FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(13190,142412,'Passage of excessively liquid or excessively frequent stools.','en',1,'2007-11-02 20:21:44',1,'2015-11-05 01:36:24','13190FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(13197,142429,'Retinopathy associated with diabetes mellitus, which may be of the background type, progressively characterized by microaneurysms, interretinal punctuate macular edema, or of the proliferative type, characterized by neovascularization of the retina and optic disk, which may project into the vitreous, proliferation of fibrous tissue, vitreous hemorrhage, and retinal detachment.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'13197FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(13227,142473,'A heterogeneous group of disorders that share glucose intolerance in common.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2019-04-03 14:40:09','13227FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(13229,142478,'Either symptomatic diabetes or impaired glucose tolerance induced by pregnancy but resolved at the end of pregnancy. It does not include previously diagnosed diabetics who become pregnant (PREGNANCY IN DIABETES).','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'13229FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(13646,143849,'Congenital malformations of organs or parts.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'13646FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(14187,145762,'Acute, localized autoinoculable infectious disease usually acquired through sexual contact. Caused by HAEMOPHILUS DUCREYI, it occurs endemically almost worldwide, especially in tropical and subtropical countries and more commonly in seaports and urban areas than in rural areas.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2016-05-21 14:01:12','14187FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(14365,146221,'Tumors or cancer of the prostate.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'14365FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(14627,147215,'The inability to see or the loss or absence of perception of visual stimuli. This condition may be the result of EYE DISEASES; OPTIC NERVE DISEASES; OPTIC CHIASM diseases; or BRAIN DISEASES affecting the VISUAL PATHWAYS or OCCIPITAL LOBE.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'14627FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(14638,147241,'Bleeding or escape of blood from a vessel.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2014-12-09 02:49:48','14638FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(14650,147277,'Mechanical or anoxic trauma incurred by the infant during labor or delivery.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'14650FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(14870,148023,'Passage of excessively liquid or excessively frequent stools.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'14870FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(14990,148353,'A genus of nematodes of the superfamily ASCARIDOIDEA whose species usually inhabit the intestine.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'14990FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15044,148531,'A recurrent disease of the oral mucosa of unknown etiology. It is characterized by small white ulcerative lesions, single or multiple, round or oval. Two to eight crops of lesions occur per year, lasting for 7 to 14 days and then heal without scarring. (From Jablonski\'s Dictionary of Dentistry, 1992, p742)','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,'2015-07-17 21:16:34','15044FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15145,148787,'Recurring attacks of transient edema suddenly appearing in areas of the skin or mucous membranes and occasionally of the viscera, often associated with dermatographism, urticaria, erythema, and purpura.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-11-05 01:32:25','15145FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15170,148888,'An acute hypersensitivity reaction due to exposure to a previously encountered antigen. The reaction may include rapidly progressing urticaria, respiratory distress, vascular collapse, systemic shock, and death.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2015-11-05 01:30:59','15170FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15309,149241,'A disease endemic among people and animals in Central Africa. It is caused by various species of trypanosomes, particularly T. gambiense and T. rhodesiense. Its second host is the tsetse fly. Involvement of the central nervous system produces \"African sleeping sickness.\" Nagana is a rapidly fatal trypanosomiasis of horses and other animals.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'15309FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15362,149496,'Inflammation of the tonsils, especially the palatine tonsils. It is often caused by a bacterium. Tonsillitis may be acute, chronic, or recurrent.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,'2012-06-27 22:37:21','15362FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15387,149579,'Inflammation of the throat.','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',1,NULL,'15387FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15491,149856,'DEF: Frequent and loose bowel movements of acute onset (< 24 hours).  DESC: Commonly associated with abdominal pain. May be associated with blood or mucus in the stool. REF: <a href=\"http://www.healthatoz.com/healthatoz/Atoz/common/standard/transform.jsp?requestURI=/healthatoz/Atoz/ency/diarrhea.jsp\"> URL</a>','en',1,'2007-10-18 04:28:24',NULL,NULL,'15491FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15878,1822,'A duration unit, 60 minutes = 1 hour.','en',1,'2009-07-06 17:27:04',NULL,NULL,'15878FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'),(15899,1854,'A qualitative assessment of the child\'s weight given his/her age. Generally, growth chart is used to identify the nutritional status.','en',1,'2009-07-14 14:07:45',NUL